# The scoreable members that deliberately do NOT ship, one per line, each with the reason it does not.
# Read by `python -m kneemri.kaggle.roster_check`, which asserts that every checkpoint under the
# processed root with a holdout record is either named in `comp/members.roster` or named HERE.
#
# WHY THE FILE EXISTS. Nothing writes the roster. A finished run leaves a checkpoint, a holdout record
# and usually a ledger section, and then somebody has to remember to type a line. On 2026-08-29 five of
# a sixteen-seat entry's best seats turned out not to be on the roster, and the sweep that followed found
# 76 scoreable members in neither file — `stackfit_s2026` at 0.8631 among them, the second-best solo the
# project owns. The fix is not "everything ships": twelve of these are smoke runs. The fix is a place to
# write down that something does not ship, so the set difference is taken by a machine and not by memory.
#
# A BARE NAME IS A FINDING TOO. `roster_check` refuses a decline with no prose, because a name alone
# records that somebody once decided and not what they decided — which is the same failure one file over.
#
# Nothing here is permanent. A decline is an argument, and it is re-opened by answering it.

# --- Below the merit level, 2026-08-30 -------------------------------------------------------------
# CORRECTION 2026-09-01 (`claims_check`): the cut is 0.8459, not 0.8460. `extended_ws_s2026` scores
# 0.845878 and the record spelled its solo three ways — 0.8459 on disk, 0.8460 here and in the ledger,
# 0.8462 on the roster line itself. One decline turned on the digit: `res392_lr8e-6_ws_s2026` reads
# 0.845878 too, TIES the merit member exactly, and was declined for being under it (knee-kpq0).
# Every member here scores below 0.8459 solo — `extended_ws_s2026`, the weakest member the roster has
# ever added on MERIT. The roster does package weaker checkpoints than these, but each of those is a
# named INSTRUMENT (the only non-DINOv2 trunk at 0.8215, the only different physical crop at 0.8345, the
# MCL specialist at 0.5332), which is a reason and not a score. So the way back onto the roster from here
# is to name the instrument the member would be, not to re-quote its number.
