                      # already been banked. Any future 224 px arm needs its own 224 px control, and
                      # base224_s2026 is not a held fit so it cannot serve as one on the gold ruler.

band224_s2026_run1    # The FIRST band224 fit, and it is declined because its record was destroyed rather
                      # than because it was priced. A duplicate arm shell survived a session boundary,
                      # started its own identical band224 run at about 18:16Z on 2026-09-05 after the
                      # first had finished, and `run_train` truncates a metrics jsonl at start - so every
                      # epoch of the completed run was overwritten and only the checkpoint remains. Its
                      # peak epoch, its trajectory and its convergence are unrecoverable, which means
                      # `convergence_check` can never certify a number quoted from it and no ledger row
                      # may cite it. `card_check` reported OK throughout: a PARKED process is invisible to
                      # it by construction, which is the hole knee-3o649 asks queue_check to close.
                      # NOT A JUDGEMENT ON THE RECIPE. The re-run under the same seed and recipe is
                      # `band224_s2026`, converged 12 of 12, and IT carries the reading: 0.8529 solo,
                      # seat -0.0002, and the 3.2x throughput result that is the arm's actual output.
                      # RE-OPEN BY: nothing. Two fits of one seeded recipe are the same experiment, and a
                      # third would only re-measure the row the re-run already holds.

rank966_hold_s2026    # The prune selector on the ruler built to see it, and it is inert. Trained from
                      # band_dense_hold with one flag changed, --label-errors pointed at the rank-966
                      # ranking (966 cells, a fifth of what errors_dense pruned). Converged 12 of 12,
                      # flag verified landed before the score was read.
                      # GOLD: 0.8862 against the control band_dense_hold_s2026 at 0.8956 over the 58
                      # annotated studies. Paired, the control leads by +0.0094 [-0.0079, +0.0260] —
                      # inside its own interval, so the arm reads FLAT and its DOWN branch is not taken.
                      # SEAT: 0.8744 (-0.0007) [-0.0011, -0.0003] against honest12 at 0.8750. Negative
                      # and outside zero; the board charges a negative at about 3x (knee-c0u9), so this
                      # is roughly -0.002 of board for a seat. Solo 0.8517, well under the pool best.
                      # The full reading is logs/rank966_hold_ledger.log.
                      # RE-OPEN BY: nothing about pruning. Two selectors that disagree about WHICH cells
                      # to drop now agree about the result of dropping them, at budgets 5.5x apart. What
                      # this does NOT answer is OVERWRITING a flagged cell — a relabelling arm that clears
                      # the gold control at 0.8956 would be a different treatment, not a re-open of this one.
                      # THAT DEFERRAL IS ANSWERED, and this line read "which no arm has run" until
                      # 2026-09-17, eleven days after the arms it was waiting for landed. Both ran
                      # 2026-09-05: `errors_relabel_s2026` (0.8522 solo, 1,932 cells corrected at the
                      # net-benefit-optimal budget, roster:710) and `relabel_hold_s2026` (gold +0.0104 with
                      # an interval crossing zero, proxy -0.0058, :569). Neither clears 0.8956, so
                      # overwriting is measured and does not pay where pruning did not. Read :569 for what
                      # the pair DID produce, which is a fact about the ruler rather than about the lever.

band224_hold_s2026    # A RULER, not a candidate. Built so that a 224 px arm could be read on the 58
                      # annotated studies against a 224 px partner — band224_s2026 is not a held fit and
                      # can never serve on that ruler. It did its job on 2026-09-05: gold 0.8940 against
                      # band_dense_hold_s2026 at 0.8956, the 336 side leading by +0.0016 [-0.0146,
                      # +0.0190], which is flat on the ruler that reads these weights 0.039 higher than
                      # the report holdout does. Proxy 0.8516. The full reading is
                      # logs/band224_hold_ledger.log.
                      # NOT PRICED AS A SEAT, deliberately. A control that shipped would stop being a
                      # control the next time the roster moved under it.
                      # RE-OPEN BY: a reason to price it, which would have to be a roster that no longer
                      # contains its 336 px twin. Nothing about the recipe: band224_s2026 already carries
                      # that reading at seat -0.0002.

relabel_hold_s2026    # The supervision arm read as a QUESTION, not as a member, and its answer is not
                      # available at the size that matters. Gold +0.0104 with an interval crossing zero,
                      # proxy -0.0058 under the 0.0062 floor: the pre-registered sign pattern, and
                      # nothing more. The binding fact it produced is about the RULER — 58 gold cells
                      # give a 95% half-width near 0.014, and the effects this project chases are 0.010,
                      # so the gold ruler cannot arbitrate supervision by construction. The full reading
                      # is logs/relabel_hold_ledger.log.
                      # AND THE BOARD HAS ALREADY ANSWERED THE CHEAP VERSION: relabel7_v1 put corrected
                      # supervision at one seat in seven and scored 0.943 against the champion 0.944.
                      # THE POWER IS NO LONGER OWNER-SIDE, AND THE ANSWER IS FLAT. The gold ruler's
                      # blindness was never the only ruler available: 410 of the 1,932 corrections land
                      # in this holdout, so the other 10,498 cells are ones the detector does not flag,
                      # where the report label is trustworthy and the ruler-bias argument cannot apply.
                      # Read there against its control band_dense_hold_s2026
                      # (`python -m kneemri.evaluation.clean_cells`), corrected supervision is
                      # +0.0005 LEDGER and -0.0005 LEDGER75 over clean cells of the 909-study fold-0
                      # holdout — opposite signs on the two cuts, a tenth of the noise floor, at 25x
                      # the gold ruler's n. THAT REFUTES THE RULER-BIAS ACCOUNT rather than confirming
                      # it: that account predicts a corrected model is better EVERYWHERE, not only on
                      # the cells it edited, and everywhere is where it is flat.
                      # The 410 flagged cells cannot arbitrate it either, in either direction — the
                      # detector selects cells where model and report disagree, so both arms read AUC
                      # 0.034/0.040 there at the midpoint, a degenerate ruler by construction.
                      # RE-OPEN BY: a correction table built by something other than model-report
                      # disagreement, since this one can only edit cells the model already had right.
                      # NOT by a full-corpus relabel — its licence was the ruler-bias account, and that
                      # is now measured false on the only population that could see it. Not by more
                      # annotated cells either: the clean cells are 181x the gold set and read zero.

band_deep224_s2026    # Depth at 224 px, one variable against band224_hold_s2026, and it is DOWN by
                      # 0.0070 (0.8446 against 0.8516) at a matched twelve-epoch budget. Under every
                      # rostered member of its own decode group (blendhold 0.8575, ema224 0.8544,
                      # labelwise224 0.8517), so it cannot seat on score, and its diversity case is
                      # nil — it is the SAME recipe as the control with a longer unfreeze ladder, which
                      # is the axis least likely to decorrelate errors. Costs 228 s an epoch against
                      # 142 for a negative delta. Full reading: logs/band_deep224_ledger.log.
                      # RE-OPEN BY: depth at 336, where the control's own advantage lives, or a ladder
                      # shape that differs in more than its length. Not by a longer budget — that moves
                      # the control too, and the epoch-budget axis is closed.

