                            # to reach it. Declined on its own refutation.
confident_span_s2026        # 0.8449 @holdout909 midpoint, ep 9 — below the pool median of 0.8470.
                            # Confidence-filtered supervision, measured, and it costs rather than pays.
chainfour_v5blend_s2026     # 0.8285 @holdout909 midpoint, ep 7, converged. The --labels v5blend arm
                            # against chainfour_s2026 0.8648: -0.0363, firing the arm's own bottom
                            # branch (<=0.8559), which closes the gold ruler as a design instrument.
                            # Declined on the SEAT too, which is the part that matters: it was the
                            # pool's strongest diversity candidate (the only member trained on that
                            # table), and LogitAverage over the top-9 honest solos prices it at
                            # -0.0019 / -0.0016 / -0.0014 at k=5/6/7, every swap-in worse still.
                            # Diversity did not rescue it. Re-open by beating the SEAT number, never
                            # by re-quoting the diversity argument.
pool_specialise_s2026       # 0.8494 @holdout909 midpoint, ep 3 of 12, converged (eight declining
                            # epochs after the peak; the one-cycle anneal e8-e11 is the four worst).
                            # Pool-then-specialise: trunk warm-started from merged3_corpus_s2026, head
                            # re-fitted on our 3,498 alone. Against control lr4e-5_ws 0.8525 that is
                            # -0.0031, inside the arm's pre-registered FLAT band, so the head-capacity
                            # explanation of merged3's column rotation is refuted and the corpus axis
                            # is closed on three agreeing numbers (+0.0043 / -0.0024 / -0.0031).
                            # Declined as a member on quality: 0.0155 under the honest solo max and a
                            # near-duplicate of the control's recipe, so no diversity argument either.
                            # Re-open only by beating the SOLO number at this corner.
moment_dense_s2026          # 0.8516 @holdout909 midpoint, ep 10 of 12, converged (three flat epochs
                            # under the one-cycle anneal). Slice pooling by the first two moments,
                            # mixed back to one vector, against calib_dense_hold 0.8634: -0.0118, the
                            # arm's own bottom band. Declined on quality: 0.0133 under the honest solo
                            # max of 0.8649, and no diversity argument survives a member that is the
                            # best corner we own minus one pooling name. The bottom band's instruction
                            # was "suspect the MIX before the mechanism" and the checkpoint dump
                            # retired both named suspects -- the spread half is alive at 0.79x the
                            # first moment's magnitude -- while surfacing the third: the identity init
                            # on the mean half washed out (mean|first-I| 0.0122 vs mean|first| 0.0135,
                            # torch.eye's own 1/768 = 0.0013), so the head was fed a learned 768x768
                            # projection of the pair, not the pair. That is a WIDTH COLLAPSE, not a
                            # verdict on the statistic, and moment_wide runs the concatenation the
                            # frozen probe actually read. Re-open only by beating the SOLO number at
                            # this corner.
soup_top5_s2026.pt          # 0.8570 @holdout909 midpoint. Uniform weight-space average of the top 5
                            # honest dense fold-0 members. -0.0079 BELOW its own best member
                            # (clean_calib_s2026 0.8649) and below all five of them. A valid network, so
                            # the members are weakly linearly mode-connected -- but a uniform soup over
                            # different recipes, label tables and anneal points lands under every member
                            # it contains. Not shippable: strictly dominated by a member already seated.
soup_top10_s2026.pt         # 0.8526, same construction at K=10. -0.0123.
soup_top20_s2026.pt         # 0.8483, same construction at K=20. -0.0166. The three read -0.0044 per
                            # doubling of K, monotone -- which is the failure mode Wortsman's GREEDY soup
                            # exists to avoid. Declined as a family, not individually: uniform souping
                            # over a top-K is refuted at this corner. A GREEDY soup is a different
                            # construction and re-opens this by measurement, not by re-quoting a number.
soup_siblings_s2026.pt      # 2-member uniform soup of stack_increments_s2026 + stack_increments_base_s2026,
                            # the tight-neighbourhood instrument: siblings that differ in one knob rather
                            # than in recipe. Built to separate "members too far apart for linear mode
                            # connectivity" from "uniform weighting is the weak form". Declined in advance
                            # of its number because it is an INSTRUMENT, not a candidate seat; if it reads
                            # above both parents this line is replaced by a roster line.
soup_siblings_s2026.pt      # MEASURED 0.8624, -0.0018 vs the better parent (stack_increments 0.8642).
                            # Lands within 0.0004 of the K-law extrapolation to K=2 (0.8628), so recipe
                            # heterogeneity is NOT what makes the uniform soup negative -- K is. Stays
                            # declined: below both parents, and it closes the weight-space axis.
fieldwide_s2026.pt          # MEASURED 0.8668 native, the best number in its own pass -- and DECLINED on
                            # both rulers that matter. Its arm's deciding reading was CROSS-SITE, and it
                            # came back FLAT: decode_cost(fieldwide) - decode_cost(labelwise_drop, its
                            # matched control) = +0.0042, inside the pre-registered -0.0049..+0.0049 flat
                            # band by 0.0008. So --scale-jitter 0.25 --padding-mode reflection is retired
                            # as a lever. As a SEAT it is worse than flat: seat_value --against
                            # cleanseat_v1 prices it +0.0008 [+0.0001, +0.0014] and calls it a TWIN
                            # (rank 0.9188, js 0.0096), and +0.0008-DISTINCT is the exact selection that
                            # labelseat_v1 shipped the day before and the board scored FLAT at 0.944.
                            # Re-open by answering the flat, not by re-quoting the 0.8668 (knee-r1w4a).

blendhold_drop40_s2026
