mergedk_labelwise_drop40_long_336_s2026
  0.8621 (l75 0.8901, e12) -- the KMAR merge carried to 336, the resolution every champion seat actually
  serves at. Its own pre-registration asked >= +0.0040 marginal over the honest core six to seat it and
  it read +0.0005 (0.9050 -> 0.9054, full 909, LogitAverage, no selection): DIRECTIONAL, NO SLOT, by the
  band the arm declared before the card was spent. The arm's fallback argument was a diversity seat, and
  that fails too on its own numbers -- rho against the six core seats spans 0.8712 to 0.9167, inside the
  ordinary range for this pool, so it is not an outlier on the axis it would have had to be one on.
  Declined as a measured null, not as a bad member: the second-site lever survives at 336 (it did not go
  negative) but it does not pay at the resolution we ship, and the 224 twin knee-dl65h should not now run.

base224_drop40_long_s2026_run1.pt       # DECLINED 2026-09-13: A SECOND RUN OF THE SAME RECIPE. It is
  `base224_drop40_long_s2026` again, flag for flag, and it reads 0.8855 ledger75 @e17 against that one's
  0.8865 @e17. Seeds are banned in this project exactly as folds are: a second draw from the same recipe
  buys no mechanism, and seating both would put two members into an ensemble whose only difference is
  initialisation noise -- the correlated-duplicate shape that makes `chainfour_up` worth +0.0007 as an
  added seat and +0.0012 as a swap.
  WHAT IT IS INSTEAD, AND IT IS NOT NOTHING: it is the operator pair's ONLY REPLICATION. +0.0070 and
  +0.0060 over the same base, a seed spread of 0.0010 against an effect of ~0.0065 -- an order of magnitude
  below it. That is the first seed-level error bar the pair has, it is quoted in knee-p29bb as the reason
  P(clears +0.0040) moved 0.6 -> 0.75, and it is why this run was worth keeping on disk. Declined as a
  SEAT, kept as EVIDENCE. Re-open only by answering the argument: name a mechanism this run carries that
  its twin does not.

labelwise_dense_drop40_long36_s2026
  The 36-epoch horizon control for labelwise_dense_drop40_long_s2026, and it answers its own question NO.
  ledger75 0.9030 (LEDGER 0.8678, best epoch 17 of 36, 909 rows) against the 24-epoch seat's ledger75
  0.9048 (LEDGER 0.8672, epoch 23): -0.0018 against the +0.003 bar knee-pqfbs pre-registered. It is
  declined as a SEAT for the plain reason that its own 24-epoch twin is already rostered and scores
  higher; a strictly-worse duplicate of a seat in the pool adds correlated error, not diversity.
  What it is as EVIDENCE: the peak at epoch 17 of 36 is the finding. The 24-epoch seat peaked at 23 of 24,
  which reads like a budget-bound run and was the whole argument for extending the horizon -- but given
  twelve more epochs the family peaks EARLIER, not later, so epoch 23 was the one_cycle anneal landing,
  not a ceiling being pushed against. The horizon lever is closed for the labelwise_*_drop40 family; the
  ext twin was killed at 00:41Z rather than spend 2 h re-measuring the same knob (knee-feb62.10).
  Re-open only by answering that: name a mechanism that makes >24 epochs pay for THIS family when its own
  36-epoch run peaked at 17.

probe224_control_s2026
  The control half of the knee-feb62.10 probe pair. 12 epochs at 224px is a gate-reading recipe, not a
  pool recipe: ledger75 0.8914 at epoch 10 against a rostered drop40_long floor of ~0.905. Declined as a
  SEAT, kept as the reference every knee-feb62.11 fragment probe is read against.

probe224_grand_s2026
  The knee-feb62.10 probe pair, built as an INSTRUMENT and never as seats: 12 epochs at 224px, which is
  a gate-reading recipe, not a pool recipe. ledger75 0.8914 (control, epoch 10) and 0.8776 (grand, epoch
  11) -- the pool's rostered drop40_long seats sit at ~0.905, so both are ~0.014-0.027 below the floor
  and would add nothing but correlated error to any ensemble. Their VALUE is the comparison between
  them: grand - control = -0.0138, which is what stopped grand_recipe from being run as a full retrain
  and what the four leave-one-out probes of knee-feb62.11 are now decomposing. Declined as SEATS, kept
  as EVIDENCE. Re-open only by answering that: name a reason a 12-epoch 224px probe belongs in a pool
  whose floor it misses by more than a board tick.

